# Sensors

Sensors are the layer that translates raw input events (pointer, keyboard, touch) into drag lifecycle calls. The library ships with two built-in sensors and exposes the `SensorDescriptor` interface so you can write your own.

## Built-in sensors

| Sensor | Activates on | Notes |
|--------|-------------|-------|
| `PointerSensor` | `pointerdown` | Handles mouse, touch, and stylus. Configurable via `startConditions` |
| `KeyboardSensor` | `Enter` / `Space` | Navigate zones with arrow keys, confirm with Enter, cancel with Escape |

Both are exported from `@horuse/svelte-dnd`.

## Default behaviour

If you do not configure `sensors` explicitly, the controller uses `[PointerSensor, KeyboardSensor]`.

Default activation rules:
- **Mouse:** drag starts after moving 5px (`Distance({ value: 5 })`)
- **Touch/Pen:** drag starts after holding 300ms with less than 8px movement (`Delay({ value: 300, tolerance: 8 })`)

## Configuring sensors

Pass configured sensors to `DndController`:

```ts
import {
    DndController,
    PointerSensor,
    KeyboardSensor,
    Distance,
    Delay,
} from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

const controller = new DndController({
    sensors: [
        new PointerSensor({
            startConditions: [
                new Distance({ value: 10 }),
                new Delay({ value: 200, tolerance: 5 }),
            ],
        }),
        new KeyboardSensor(),
    ],
});
```

> **Note:** `KeyboardSensor` is now self-contained — no controller reference needed.

## Start conditions

`startConditions` is an array of `StartCondition` objects. The drag starts when **any** condition is `satisfied`. If **all** conditions are `aborted` (e.g. user scrolled), the activation is cancelled.

### Distance

Activates after the pointer moves a certain number of pixels:

```ts
new Distance({ value: 5 })
// With tolerance — aborts if movement exceeds this threshold
new Distance({ value: 5, tolerance: 50 })
```

### Delay

Activates after holding the pointer for a duration (useful for touch to distinguish from scroll):

```ts
new Delay({ value: 300, tolerance: 8 })
// value: hold duration in ms
// tolerance: max movement in px during delay before aborting
```

### Combining conditions

```ts
// Drag starts after 5px movement OR after 300ms hold
new PointerSensor({
    startConditions: [
        new Distance({ value: 5 }),
        new Delay({ value: 300, tolerance: 8 }),
    ],
})
```

### Per-pointer-type logic

`startConditions` can be a function that receives the `PointerEvent` and returns conditions based on pointer type:

```ts
new PointerSensor({
    startConditions(event) {
        switch (event.pointerType) {
            case 'mouse':
                return [new Distance({ value: 5 })];
            case 'touch':
                return [new Delay({ value: 250, tolerance: 5 })];
            default:
                return [
                    new Distance({ value: 5 }),
                    new Delay({ value: 200, tolerance: 10 }),
                ];
        }
    },
})
```

## Pointer-only (disable keyboard)

```ts
const controller = new DndController({
    sensors: [new PointerSensor()],
});
```

## Per-item sensor override

You can override sensors on individual draggable items using the `sensors` prop on `DndDraggable`:

```svelte
<DndDraggable id={item.id} {position} sensors={[new PointerSensor({ startConditions: [new Distance({ value: 10 })] })]}>
    {item.label}
</DndDraggable>
```

The per-item sensors take precedence over controller-level sensors for that element.

## Custom start condition

Implement `StartCondition` to create your own activation rule:

```ts
import type { StartCondition, ActivationState, ConditionResult } from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

const doubleTap: StartCondition = {
    evaluate(state: ActivationState): ConditionResult {
        // Custom logic — activate on specific condition
        if (state.elapsedMs > 500) return 'aborted';
        // ... your check here
        return 'pending';
    },
    // Optional: tell the sensor to re-evaluate after this duration
    getRequiredDuration() {
        return 500;
    },
};

new PointerSensor({ startConditions: [doubleTap] })
```

## Custom sensor

Implement `SensorDescriptor` to create your own input sensor:

```ts
import type { SensorDescriptor, SensorActivation, SensorCallbacks } from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

const mySensor: SensorDescriptor = {
    activate(event, element, callbacks): SensorActivation | null {
        // Return null if this sensor doesn't handle the event
        if (!(event instanceof CustomEvent)) return null;

        // Start drag immediately
        callbacks.onStart({ x: 0, y: 0 });

        return {
            initialTransform: { x: 0, y: 0 },
            offset: { x: 0, y: 0 },
            destroy() {
                // Clean up any listeners added here
            },
        };
    },
};

const controller = new DndController({ sensors: [mySensor] });
```

## KeyboardSensor navigation

Once activated (Enter or Space on a focused draggable), keyboard navigation works as follows:

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `ArrowDown` / `ArrowRight` | Move to next position in current container |
| `ArrowUp` / `ArrowLeft` | Move to previous position in current container |
| `ArrowRight` (at last item) | Jump to first position in next container |
| `ArrowLeft` (at first item) | Jump to last position in previous container |
| `Enter` | Confirm drop at current preview position |
| `Escape` | Cancel drag, ghost returns to origin |

## Types

```ts
interface SensorDescriptor {
    activate(
        event: Event,
        element: HTMLElement,
        callbacks: SensorCallbacks
    ): SensorActivation | null;
}

interface StartCondition {
    evaluate(state: ActivationState): ConditionResult;
    getRequiredDuration?(): number | null;
}

type StartConditionInput =
    | StartCondition[]
    | ((event: PointerEvent) => StartCondition[]);

interface PointerSensorOptions {
    startConditions?: StartConditionInput;
}

interface ActivationState {
    startX: number;
    startY: number;
    currentX: number;
    currentY: number;
    elapsedMs: number;
    pointerType: 'mouse' | 'touch' | 'pen';
}

type ConditionResult = 'satisfied' | 'pending' | 'aborted';

type NavigationDirection = 'up' | 'down' | 'left' | 'right';

interface SensorCallbacks {
    onStart(initialTransform: { x: number; y: number }): void;
    onMove(transform: { x: number; y: number }, mouseX: number, mouseY: number): void;
    onEnd(): void;
    onCancel(): void;
    onNavigate?(direction: NavigationDirection): void;
}

interface SensorActivation {
    initialTransform: { x: number; y: number };
    offset: { x: number; y: number };
    destroy(): void;
}
```

